IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rtad-drivers`

-- Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 (WA) and Regulations 2014, ss 2, 10, 16-18, 23, 24, 40-52, 66; r 4, 9-11, 15, 16A, 35, 36, 43, 44, 47, 53B-53C, 55, 57, 65; Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The figures come from the deposited Act, Regulations
-- and Road Traffic Code 2000; nothing here has been checked against a decided case.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_road-traffic-authorisation-to-drive-act-2008_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts used are from the workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-{chloe,jake,daniel}/facts.json: Chloe born
-- 14 March 2003 (c021 permit 14 March 2019, c022 licence 14 March 2020); Jake born 30 August 2006 (k032 licence 30 August
-- 2023, k083 25 km/h over on a motorcycle 19 July 2049); Daniel's permit d012 15 October 2012. HYPOTHETICAL: Chloe's
-- supervisor (her father, licensed 30 years), her logbook hours and test dates, her passengers, Jake's motorcycle licence
-- and its condition S, and the day of any notice to Jake. That 19 July 2049 is not in a holiday period is an INFERENCE (no
-- WA public holiday falls near it; the Public and Bank Holidays Act 1972 was not read).

§ `fixtures`

`Chloe driving with her father beside her` MEANS `My learning drive` WITH
    `my permit is in force` IS TRUE
    `I am driving solely to learn` IS TRUE
    `my supervisor` IS `another licensed driver`
    `years my supervisor has held a licence for this kind of driving` IS 30
    `I am learning to ride a moped` IS FALSE
    `my supervisor accompanies me` IS TRUE

`Chloe driving alone on her permit` MEANS `My learning drive` WITH
    `my permit is in force` IS TRUE
    `I am driving solely to learn` IS TRUE
    `my supervisor` IS `another licensed driver`
    `years my supervisor has held a licence for this kind of driving` IS 30
    `I am learning to ride a moped` IS FALSE
    `my supervisor accompanies me` IS FALSE

`Chloe's logbook and tests` MEANS `My driving experience` WITH
    `my date of birth` IS (Date 14 3 2003)
    `the day my learner's permit was granted` IS (Date 14 3 2019)
    `supervised hours logged` IS 52
    `of them, night hours` IS 6
    `logged in an approved logbook, signed by my supervisors` IS TRUE
    `I passed the hazard perception test` IS TRUE
    `the day of the hazard perception test` IS (Date 16 9 2019)
    `I passed the practical driving assessment` IS TRUE
    `the day of the practical driving assessment` IS (Date 14 3 2020)

`Chloe's hazard test taken too early` MEANS `My driving experience` WITH
    `my date of birth` IS (Date 14 3 2003)
    `the day my learner's permit was granted` IS (Date 14 3 2019)
    `supervised hours logged` IS 52
    `of them, night hours` IS 6
    `logged in an approved logbook, signed by my supervisors` IS TRUE
    `I passed the hazard perception test` IS TRUE
    `the day of the hazard perception test` IS (Date 13 9 2019)
    `I passed the practical driving assessment` IS TRUE
    `the day of the practical driving assessment` IS (Date 14 3 2020)

`three school friends` MEANS `My passengers` WITH
    `number of passengers, counting any co-driver` IS 3
    `years the most experienced passenger has held a non-provisional licence for my class` IS 0
    `every passenger after the first is immediate family` IS FALSE
    `my employer requires me to carry them, and I carry the employer's signed document` IS FALSE

`three of my own family` MEANS `My passengers` WITH
    `number of passengers, counting any co-driver` IS 3
    `years the most experienced passenger has held a non-provisional licence for my class` IS 0
    `every passenger after the first is immediate family` IS TRUE
    `my employer requires me to carry them, and I carry the employer's signed document` IS FALSE

`Jake riding his motorcycle on his licence` MEANS `My drive` WITH
    `my licence or permit covers this class of vehicle` IS TRUE
    `it is current, not suspended or cancelled, and not obtained while disqualified` IS TRUE
    `I am disqualified from holding or obtaining a licence` IS FALSE
    `I am breaking a Schedule 7 condition (A, B, E, I, N, S or Z)` IS FALSE
    `I am breaking a novice night-time or passenger restriction` IS FALSE
    `on a learner's permit, my supervisor is with me or I hold no permit` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle needs no licence under r 55` IS FALSE
    `the CEO gave me a written permit for this driving` IS FALSE

`Jake riding without the glasses his condition S requires` MEANS `My drive` WITH
    `my licence or permit covers this class of vehicle` IS TRUE
    `it is current, not suspended or cancelled, and not obtained while disqualified` IS TRUE
    `I am disqualified from holding or obtaining a licence` IS FALSE
    `I am breaking a Schedule 7 condition (A, B, E, I, N, S or Z)` IS TRUE
    `I am breaking a novice night-time or passenger restriction` IS FALSE
    `on a learner's permit, my supervisor is with me or I hold no permit` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle needs no licence under r 55` IS FALSE
    `the CEO gave me a written permit for this driving` IS FALSE

`Jake riding while disqualified` MEANS `My drive` WITH
    `my licence or permit covers this class of vehicle` IS TRUE
    `it is current, not suspended or cancelled, and not obtained while disqualified` IS TRUE
    `I am disqualified from holding or obtaining a licence` IS TRUE
    `I am breaking a Schedule 7 condition (A, B, E, I, N, S or Z)` IS FALSE
    `I am breaking a novice night-time or passenger restriction` IS FALSE
    `on a learner's permit, my supervisor is with me or I hold no permit` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle needs no licence under r 55` IS FALSE
    `the CEO gave me a written permit for this driving` IS FALSE

§ `s 2, s 66 -- d012: Daniel's 2012 permit came before the Act`

#ASSERT NOT `Does this Act govern my authorisation to drive on` (Date 15 10 2012)
#ASSERT `Does this Act govern my authorisation to drive on` (Date 14 3 2019)

#ASSERT `Is my old permit taken to be a learner's permit under this Act` TRUE TRUE

§ `r 44, s 10, s 11A -- c021: Chloe turns 16 and gets a learner's permit`

#ASSERT `Am I old enough to hold a learner's permit` (Date 14 3 2003) (Date 14 3 2019) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I old enough to hold a learner's permit` (Date 14 3 2003) (Date 13 3 2019) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I old enough to hold a learner's permit` (Date 14 3 2003) (Date 14 9 2018) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I old enough to hold a learner's permit` (Date 14 3 2003) (Date 1 1 2018) FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `Can I be issued a learner's permit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, if the CEO decides to issue it`
#ASSERT `Can I be issued a learner's permit` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not yet: I must first show knowledge of the traffic laws (the theory test)`

#ASSERT `Is my learner's permit in force` (Date 14 3 2019) (Date 14 3 2022) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my learner's permit in force` (Date 14 3 2019) (Date 15 3 2022) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my learner's permit in force` (Date 14 3 2019) (Date 15 3 2020) FALSE TRUE

